an citizen  had made a deal with the liberian  government he created  a company an american-based company  based here in virginia  that was to be the exclusive middleman  between any international corporation  and the government of liberia basically  if anyone wanted to set up their  corporation in liberia  they would have to go through this guy  and his new company he helped the  liberian government craft  laws that would make it very attractive  for people  to put the liberian flag on their ship  or  on their company and over the next few  years this gained  major traction at this time any shipping  vessel  that had the american flag or the soviet  flag  would be subject to a bunch of trade  barriers that were starting to go up as  a part of this like cold war between the  us and soviets  this ex-secretary of state and his new  company would go around and say hey put  the liberian flag on your ship  and now you can trade with whoever the  hell you want the liberian registry  exploded  and now you had ships flying the  liberian flag not having to pay barely  any taxes and not having to obey  any laws from the united states and  being able to trade with whomever they  want  because liberia was officially neutral  in the cold war the liberian registry  was born  and it was thriving  so in recent decades the number of ships  that register under the liberian flag  who never stepped foot in liberia by the  way  but have their flag on their ship has  grown and has become  the second most common flag on  international ships in the world only  second to panama  meanwhile the company here in virginia  who has a monopoly over this  registry is getting super rich and  they're giving some of those riches to  the liberian government  but what the liberian government does  with that money is actually  probably the ugliest underbelly of this  whole story  so by the late 90s this company's doing  great liberia's  taking in a bunch of money from all of  the ships registering under their flag  but then  this guy charles taylor becomes the  president  how can i help you on liberian shipping  registries it's a long time since i've  been looking at them  what has the registry allowed the  government of liberia  to do that it wouldn't be able to do  otherwise it was one of the most  consistent  dependable sources of revenue for the  liberian government that was important  particularly in the charles taylor  period when it was civil war  in in liberia and there were no other  sources of revenue  it was a war economy he  starts taking the money that's coming in  from all these ship and corporation  registries  but not just to fight these wars he goes  on to commit some of the most egregious  crimes the world has ever seen  as the one myself that investigated the  shipping registry  we found documented exposed that the  shipping registry  that its revenues were being diverted to  purchase arms and ammunition in  violation of u.n sanctions  and yet the corporations and ships that  fly the liberian flag  don't even have to think about this  stuff they don't step foot in liberia  they've never met charles taylor or any  of his people  they just go about doing their thing and  doing all of their business  through a nondescript office  right near my house where a company is  getting  very rich using liberia as  the facade but really everything is  happening  right here the money is being made right  here and a little bit of that  is being sent to liberia and liberia is  using it to do terrible things  charles taylor eventually goes to the  international court of justice and  gets indicted on a million really  horrible counts goes to joe for the rest  of his life  but the registry that helped fund  his horrible rise remains  and remains as a mechanism  for helping many corporations around the  world hide their secrets  and evade accountability and this  connection between these  two unlikely places retains a similar  purpose  as its original one way back in the  1800s when with the support of the u.s  government  private interests sent away their  secrets  and their guilt to a far away place and  that hasn't really stopped happening  today with the blessing of the u.s  government corporations  continue to deposit their secrets in  this same  faraway place far away from any real  accountability  thank you all for watching this video  this is the type of video that i want to  do more of  a video like this takes longer takes  more time because it's a lot more  research it's more interviews  i'm actually diving way deeper into  these stories than  than the typical explainer you see on  this channel and that's what i want to  do  starting in 2021 i want to start doing  more stories like this  my patrons make that possible and brands  like fully who  care about this sort of thing make that  possible as well so  i am hoping that more and more i'll be  able to  do deep dive stories like this and then  when travel opens up i want to be able  to travel  and go do deep dive stuff like i used to  do it at vox  um thank you all for watching and i've  got some more good stuff coming  and i hope you are having a wonderful  november and i'll  see you soon
 

